# Source screenshot captures for the app pages.
#
# The JPEGs committed in img/ are generated from these at the width the pages
# actually render — 7.5 MB of PNG becomes about 1.1 MB of JPEG. The originals are
# deliberately kept out of git: once committed they stay in history for good, even
# if deleted later, and nothing on the site ever serves them.
img/rackviewerscreenshot*.png

# Source GIF captures of the video mode, 56 MB between them. What ships is
# img/rackviewer-video.mp4, encoded from rackviewergif2.gif: same resolution and
# frame rate at 1.31 MB, because h264 is not stuck with a 256-colour palette.
img/rackviewergif*.gif

# Rendered intro cards. brand/make_intro.py regenerates them in seconds, and video that
# the site does not serve has no business in git. See what 56 MB of unreferenced GIFs
# cost to remove from history.
brand/*.mp4

# The Rack Detector shots (img/rackdetectorscreenshot*.png) are committed as PNG on
# purpose - do not "fix" this for consistency. Those are flat-colour UI captures, not
# photographs: JPEG re-encoding came out 2-42% LARGER on every one of them, and softened
# the log text that is the whole reason for showing the window.
